          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Using the formula</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^N n^2 \t= \\frac{1}{6}N(N+1)(2N+1)]</span></p><p>with <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N=100,]</span> we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(100)n^{2}|= (1)/(6) \u22c5 100(100 + 1)(2 \u22c5 100 + 1); = (1)/(6) \u22c5 100 \u22c5 101 \u22c5 201; = 338350.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Using the formula\n\n[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^N n^2 = \\frac{1}{6}N(N+1)(2N+1)]\n\nwith [MATH: N=100,] we get\n\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(100)n^{2}|= (1)/(6) \u22c5 100(100 + 1)(2 \u22c5 100 + 1); = (1)/(6) \u22c5 100 \u22c5 101 \u22c5 201; = 338350.]",
