          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we take the factor <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> outside the summation:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^{100} 4n^2 \t= 4\\sum_{n=1}^{100} n^2]</span></p><p>Now, using the formula</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^N n^2 \t= \\frac{1}{6}N(N+1)(2N+1)]</span></p><p>with <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N=100,]</span> we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4\u2211_(n = 1)^(100)n^{2}|= 4((1)/(6) \u22c5 100(100 + 1)(2 \u22c5 100 + 1)); = 4 \u22c5 (1)/(6) \u22c5 100 \u22c5 101 \u22c5 201; = 4 \u22c5 338350; = 1353400.]</span></p>",
