        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nCalculate\n[MATH: \\displaystyle\n\\sum_{n=1}^{50} (3n^2+2n).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nNotice that we can write the given summation as follows:\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)(3n^{2} + 2n)|= \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)3n^{2} + \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)2n; = 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n^{2} + 2\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n]\n\nNow, let's evaluate the two series using our formulas.\n\n- For the first series, we use the formula\n[MATH: \\displaystyle \\sum_{n=1}^N n^2 = \\dfrac1 6 N (N+1)(2N+1)]\nwith [MATH: N=50,] and we get\n[MATH: 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n^{2}|= 3((1)/(6) \u22c5 50(50 + 1)(2 \u22c5 50 + 1)); = 3 \u22c5 (1)/(6) \u22c5 50 \u22c5 51 \u22c5 101; = 3 \u22c5 42925; = 128775.]\n- For the second series, we use the formula\n[MATH: \\displaystyle \\sum_{n=1}^N n = \\dfrac1 2 N (N+1)]\nwith [MATH: N=50,] and we get\n[MATH: 2\u2211_(n = 1)^(50)n|= 2((1)/(2) \u22c5 50 \u22c5 (50 + 1)); = 2 \u22c5 1275; = 2550.]\n\nFinally, we have\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(50)(3n^{2} + 2n)|= 128775 + 2550; = 131325.]"
